From 4e569a8ff4c28842365ad914bd92579d242f406a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bakhodirovxz <bohodirovasadbek1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:55:11 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/19] calc: hold a recalculation pass in per-column slots,
 not hash maps

A pass held three maps sized to every formula it calculates: the trees
(`exprs`), the results and the pending set. Opening a workbook calculates
every formula, so they were the largest part of the peak: about 125 bytes
per formula, 430 MB for 3.5 million.

Keep one slot per formula instead, in a vector per column from its first
formula of the pass to its last when they are dense (a filled-down
column), else a map of rows: 24 bytes per formula. The trees are not held
at all: the workbook doesn't change during a pass, so each formula's tree
is taken from its cell when it is calculated, as the pass already built a
shifted copy's tree then.

The pass calculates the same formulas in the same order; only where it
keeps them changed.
